  "content": {
    "id": "v2-55815-p13-practice-slot-6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "A café recorded the number of coffees sold in each hour of a 10-hour trading day.\n\n$12,\\ 15,\\ 9,\\ 14,\\ 11,\\ 16,\\ 13,\\ 10,\\ 12,\\ 8$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "v2-55815-p13-practice-slot-6-slot-6-q-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Calculate the mean and population standard deviation for these sales. Answer correct to one decimal place.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\mu=12.0,\\quad\\sigma=2.4$ coffees.",
          "worked": "There are $10$ values, with $\\sum x=120$ and $\\sum x^2=1500$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\mu&=\\frac{120}{10}\\\\\\mu&=12\\\\\\sigma&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1500}{10}-12^2}\\\\\\sigma&=\\sqrt6\\\\\\sigma&\\approx2.4\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-55815-p13-practice-slot-6-slot-6-q-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "What is the z-score of the hour with the highest sales? Answer to 1 d.p.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1.6$",
          "worked": "The highest value is $16$. Using the unrounded standard deviation from part a:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}z&=\\frac{x-\\mu}{\\sigma}\\\\z&=\\frac{16-12}{\\sqrt6}\\\\z&\\approx1.6\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-55815-p13-practice-slot-6-slot-6-q-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "During a street festival, the sales in one hour were 2.2 standard deviations above the mean. How many coffees were sold in that hour? Answer to 1 decimal place.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$17.4$ coffees.",
          "worked": "Here $z=2.2$. Using the unrounded statistics:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\mu+z\\sigma\\\\x&=12+2.2\\sqrt6\\\\x&\\approx17.4\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
  },
